<title>MEXICO: Penoles outlines own-mines refinery intake.</title>
<headline>Penoles outlines own-mines refinery intake.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-03-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's Industrias Penoles, the world's largest refined silver producer, outlined plans to increase its owned-mined volumes of metal ores to be processed at its smelters and refineries.</p>
<p>Below is a table of the changes planned in its mining division over the period 1996-2000, figures in percentages.</p>
<p>The 2000 goal includes three future mines. No other details were given.</p>
<p>  Metal			   1996		     2000</p>
<p>  Gold			     44			 73</p>
<p>  Silver			   52			 59</p>
<p>  Lead			     38			 38</p>
<p>  Zinc			     71			 85</p>
<p>Penoles said the above outlook table does not include or consider potential acquisitions, development of new businesses nor prospects under exploration.</p>
<p>((--Chris Aspin, Mexico City newsroom +525 7287902))</p>
</text>
